{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "JAS",
  "chapter": 4,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "JAS.4.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.4.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "From whence ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "come",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " wars and fightings among you? ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "come they",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not hence, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " from your lusts that war in your members?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.4.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.4.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Ye lust and have not: ye kill, and desire to have, and cannot obtain: ye fight and war, yet ye have not, because ye ask not.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.4.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.4.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Ye ask, and receive not, because ye ask amiss, that ye may consume ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " upon your lusts.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.4.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.4.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Ye adulterers and adulteresses, know ye not that the friendship of the world is enmity with God? whoever therefore will be a friend of the world is the enemy of God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.4.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.4.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Do ye think that the scripture saith in vain, The spirit that dwelleth in us lusteth to envy?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.4.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.4.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But he giveth more grace. Wherefore he saith, God resisteth the proud, but giveth grace to the humble.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.4.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.4.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Submit yourselves therefore to God. Resist the devil, and he will flee from you.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.4.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.4.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Draw nigh to God, and he will draw nigh to you. Cleanse ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "your",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " hands, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "ye",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " sinners, and purify ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "your",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " hearts, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "ye",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " double-minded.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.4.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.4.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Be afflicted, and mourn, and weep: let your laughter be turned to mourning, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "your",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " joy to heaviness.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.4.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.4.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Humble yourselves in the sight of the Lord, and he will lift you up.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.4.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.4.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Speak not evil one of another, brethren. He that speaketh evil of ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "his",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " brother, and judgeth his brother, speaketh evil of the law, and judgeth the law: but if thou judgest the law, thou art not a doer of the law, but a judge.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.4.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.4.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "There is one lawgiver, who is able to save, and to destroy: who art thou that judgest another?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.4.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.4.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Come now, ye that say, To-day or to-morrow we will go into such a city, and continue there a year, and buy, and sell, and get gain:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.4.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.4.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Whereas ye know not what ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "will be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " on the morrow: For what ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " your life? It is even a vapor, that appeareth for a little time, and then vanisheth away.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.4.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.4.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Instead of that ye ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "ought",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to say, If the Lord will, we shall live, and do this, or that.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.4.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.4.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But now ye rejoice in your boastings: all such rejoicing is evil.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JAS.4.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JAS.4.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore to him that knoweth to do good, and doeth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not, to him it is sin.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
